{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If size is larger than the length of data, yield one chunk containing all data.\n    The final chunk may be smaller than size if data length is not a multiple of size.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or str): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        bytes or str: Chunks of the input data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"chunk size must be positive\")\n\n    length = len(data)\n    if size >= length:\n        yield data\n        return\n\n    for start in range(0, length, size):\n        # Always yield the chunk, even if smaller than size\n        yield data[start:start + size]\n","expected_sha256":"99cc97636196063d06f8223da4d9ce631cab590ebde505f417f079537a308e5f","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"The original code already yields the final partial chunk correctly, but the previous fix attempts may have altered behavior. This version keeps the original logic, which yields all chunks including the final partial one, and yields the entire data if size >= length, satisfying the requirements."}